tasqx mcp: serving over stdio (scope=read)
{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"tools":{}},"instructions":"tasqx is this workspace's organiser: its backlog, and its long-term memory, one searchable index over imported knowledge docs and the annotations written on tasks. Use it instead of an in-conversation todo list or a memory file.\n\nSearch first. Call tasqx_search_memory before resuming work, choosing between designs, touching a convention-bearing file, or asserting how this project does something. Query with two or three keywords, never a sentence: every word is required, and `matched` shows what ran. Try a second wording before concluding nothing is there. A hit is a snippet: read a doc whole with tasqx_get_memory, and an annotation (source `task:#<id>`) with tasqx_get_task.\n\nThis server is read-only: no write tool is listed. Say so once, keep searching, and put what you would have stored (decisions and their reasons, outcomes, conventions) into your reply rather than dropping it. The operator grants writes by relaunching with `tasqx mcp serve --scope write`.\n\nAn empty store is a store nobody seeded. If searches keep returning nothing, ask the user to run `tasqx memory import <docs-dir>` once per markdown folder; no MCP tool imports. The CLI is always `tasqx <verb>`: a bare `tasqx` opens a full-screen dashboard and hangs a tool call. Tool descriptions here are deliberately short and state only the contract; the reasoning behind a rule is in DESIGN.md §12 under the D-number the description cites, which tasqx_search_memory finds once those docs are imported (D155).\n\nNo code mapper on PATH: tell the user once that `tasqx setup` shows how to install ripwire.\n\nRecent notes for project website (context, not rulings):\n- pricing-page-decisions: # Pricing page Three tiers, annual billing shown first. The release of v2 waits for legal to sign off the new terms.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","serverInfo":{"name":"tasqx","version":"0.14.0"}}}
{"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"tools":[{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_list_tasks"},"description":"List tasks matching a filter-DSL query — the CLI's grammar, e.g. \"project:work status:pending +api due.before:tomorrow\". Paged: the response carries `count`, `total` and `next_offset`, null once nothing is left. Rows carry a default field set unless you name `fields` (D152).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"fields":{"description":"Restrict each row to these fields. Omit for short_id, title, status, priority, urgency, blocked, due, project, tags, with null-valued keys dropped; send [] for the whole row.","items":{"enum":["_rev","active_since","blocked","budget_tokens","completed","created","depends_on","due","estimate","id","modified","priority","project","recurrence","remind","scheduled","short_id","status","status_unrecognized","tags","title","tokens","tracked","tracked_adjustment","urgency","wait"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"filter":{"description":"Filter DSL, e.g. \"status:pending +api\". \"@working\" is the actionable set. Omit it (or send \"\") for every task.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Rows to return. Omit for this tool's page (100), shrunk to fit the response byte budget; a named limit is honoured up to 10000.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"Matching rows to skip; pass the previous `next_offset`. Ordering is stable across pages.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"sort":{"description":"Sort keys, e.g. [\"-urgency\", \"due\"]; \"-\" descends. Valid: urgency, short_id, priority, due, created, modified, title, tokens, estimate, tracked. An unknown key is rejected.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_list_tasks"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_get_task"},"description":"Get one task's full detail: fields, tags, annotations, dependencies. Annotations come back in pages counted from the newest, oldest first within a page — the response carries `annotations_total`, and `annotations_next_offset` whenever older ones were left out.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"annotations_limit":{"description":"Most-recent annotations to return; omit for this tool's page (20). An over-budget page is cut to what fits and the view names the `annotations_offset` for the rest; `include_json: true` spends that budget first. 0 returns none.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"annotations_offset":{"description":"Annotations to skip, counted back from the newest; pass the previous `annotations_next_offset`.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"explain":{"description":"Add `urgency_breakdown` (`priority`, `due_proximity`, `age`, `total`) — the terms `urgency` sums (D1). Default false.","type":"boolean"},"include_json":{"description":"Send the machine-readable JSON block beside the rendered view. Default FALSE: it is one result twice and you read the view (D151). True when a SCRIPT parses this.","type":"boolean"},"max_body_bytes":{"description":"Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id (integer) or full UUID (string).","type":["integer","string"]},"view":{"description":"How the rendered block is spelled. Default \"markdown\", the view YOU read; \"card\" is the D146 72-column box card in a text fence, for a PERSON deciding on the task (D164), and quotes only the first annotation.","enum":["markdown","card"],"type":"string"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_get_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_brief_task"},"description":"Everything you need before starting one task, in ONE call (D136): the task, the tasks it depends on with what each of THEM concluded, what it blocks, and memory found under a query tasqx derives from the task's title, tags and project. Use tasqx_get_task when you only need the task.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_json":{"description":"Send the machine-readable JSON block beside the rendered view. Default FALSE: it is the brief again, snippets included (D151). True when a script parses this.","type":"boolean"},"include_rank":{"description":"Add the raw FTS5 bm25 `rank` to each memory hit; default false, and visible only in the `include_json` block. LOWER is the better match and hits arrive sorted best-first.","type":"boolean"},"max_body_bytes":{"description":"Cap each annotation body at this many BYTES in the response; default 16384. A longer body is cut on a character boundary and marked with its real size and the call that reads it whole; the store is never capped (D148).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"memory_limit":{"description":"Memory hits to return; default 5. Half the slots (rounded up) are reserved for knowledge docs, annotations fill the rest, and either kind takes the other's unused slots.","type":"integer"},"ref":{"description":"Task short_id or UUID.","type":["integer","string"]},"view":{"description":"How the TASK HALF is spelled. Default \"markdown\", the view YOU read; \"card\" is the D146 72-column box card in a text fence, for a PERSON deciding on the task (D164). Prerequisites and memory hits stay markdown.","enum":["markdown","card"],"type":"string"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_brief_task"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_summary"},"description":"Aggregate report grouped by project, status or priority. Pure read.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"all":{"description":"Count cancelled tasks too. By default a report with no status term skips cancelled only — done work always counts (D24).","type":"boolean"},"filter":{"description":"Optional filter DSL to scope the report.","type":"string"},"group_by":{"description":"Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.","enum":["project","status","priority"],"type":"string"},"metrics":{"description":"Extra columns per group. Omit and each group carries only `count`: every other metric is opt-in here, unlike `tasqx report`.","items":{"enum":["count","est_total","overdue","tracked_total","tokens_in","tokens_out","tokens_cache_read","tokens_cache_creation","tokens_unsplit"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"since":{"description":"Window `tracked_total` and the token buckets to spend at or after this instant, not the task's lifetime total — a different axis from `filter`'s `completed.*` terms (D97).","type":"string"},"until":{"description":"The other end of `since`: excludes anything at or after this instant. Together they window WHEN the spend happened.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_summary"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_outcomes"},"description":"How the work went rather than what it cost: rework, estimate calibration, token cost, unannotated completions, started-then-cancelled work, and `forced` (completions that overrode open blockers). Every rate carries the `n` it was computed over. Scope is tasks that CLOSED; `tasqx_summary` reads work in flight.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"filter":{"description":"Optional filter DSL to scope the report — `tasqx_list_tasks`' grammar.","type":"string"},"group_by":{"description":"Grouping axis. Optional; defaults to project.","enum":["project","status","priority"],"type":"string"},"metrics":{"description":"Which metrics to emit. Omit for ALL of them; naming none does not mean a bare count here.","items":{"enum":["rework","calibration","cost","silent","abandonment","overrun","unproven","forced"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"since":{"description":"Only count tasks that closed at or after this instant. `since`/`until` window WHEN THE TASK CLOSED, not when spend happened.","type":"string"},"until":{"description":"The other end of `since`: excludes tasks that closed at or after this instant.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_outcomes"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_list_projects"},"description":"List projects. By default excludes archived projects.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_archived":{"type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_list_projects"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_search_memory"},"description":"Search the memory store — imported docs and task annotations — bm25-ranked with snippets. A plain query is matched as phrases by word STEM and every word is REQUIRED, so `matched` explains a zero-hit answer; `raw: true` takes FTS5 syntax instead. A hit is an excerpt: `tasqx_get_memory` reads a doc whole, `tasqx_get_task` an annotation. `hits` is sorted best-first (LOWER bm25 `rank` is better); `total` and `has_more` say what `limit` cut. A doc hit adds `stale` (D180).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_rank":{"description":"Add the raw FTS5 bm25 `rank` to each hit. Default false. LOWER (more negative) is better and `hits` is already sorted best-first, so never use it as a threshold (D154).","type":"boolean"},"include_unscoped":{"description":"Widen a `project` scope to docs and annotations with NO project — what `tasqx memory import` produces. Never admits another project's. Refused without `project`.","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Max hits (0 or more); default 10. The response's `total`/`has_more` say what this left out.","type":"integer"},"project":{"description":"Scope to one project: docs stored with it, and annotations whose task carries it. Omit to search every project.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"Plain-text search words. Matched as quoted phrases, so hyphens and dots are safe.","type":"string"},"raw":{"description":"Pass the query through as FTS5 syntax. Invalid syntax is refused as bad_request.","type":"boolean"},"scope":{"description":"What to search. Optional; defaults to all.","enum":["all","docs","annotations"],"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_search_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_list_memory"},"description":"Browse memory docs without knowing a word inside one — what `tasqx_search_memory` cannot do without a query. Newest-modified first, paged like `tasqx_list_tasks`. A row is `id`, `title`, `source` and `modified`, enough to RECOGNISE a doc; `include_preview: true` adds the rest, and `tasqx_get_memory` reads one whole (D154).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"include_preview":{"description":"Return the whole engine row — `project`, `created`, `_rev`, a 160-character `body_preview`, `body_truncated` — instead of the four identifying fields. Default false (D154).","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Rows to return; default 20, because an unbounded browse page grows with the store.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"Matching docs to skip; pass the previous response's `next_offset`.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"project":{"description":"Restrict to docs stored with this `project`. Omit to list every doc.","type":"string"},"standing":{"description":"true lists only standing docs, false only the rest; omit for all (D156).","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_list_memory"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"tasqx_get_memory"},"description":"Read one knowledge doc whole, by the `id` a search hit carries — `tasqx_search_memory` returns only an excerpt. An annotation id is refused, naming the task to read it from instead.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"id":{"description":"The doc UUID, as a search hit or `tasqx_add_memory` prints it.","type":"string"}},"required":["id"],"type":"object"},"name":"tasqx_get_memory"}]}}
